{
 "note": "Round V, lane VP: the avatar's perfect-parry and perfect-dodge motions (review/v/ref_pd.md 4), one body track for all seven characters. Authored like the other clips (-Z forward, right = -X, torso / root negative X leans forward, arm / leg positive X swings forward, right arm positive Z crosses the body). Sparse keys; tools/build_player_beat.mjs samples every tick, solves the weapon so its blade points along `blade` (a direction in the same frame; `blade: \"arm\"` = along the forearm) and feeds the dense clips to build_player_rig.mjs (rig characters: clips pparry / pparry_i / pdodge / pdodge_i) and to the stand-in rig of the mannequin characters (char/motion/lite). Ticks are real game ticks: pparry starts on the contact tick, pdodge 5 ticks after the dodged hit (the slow motion is authored slow: ticks 1-9 are the x1/3 beat). `ground` lists tick ranges in which the lower foot is put exactly on the floor (shift Y is solved; the authored value is ignored there).",
